Which of the following conditioning regimens is not commonly used for myeloablative conditioning (MAC)?
(1) TBI 2 Gy bid x 3 days, Cyclophosphamide 60mg/kgBW/day x 2 days;
(2) Fludarabine 30 mg/m2/day x 5 days, Cyclophosphamide 14.5 mg/kgBW/day x 2 days, TBI 2Gy x 1 day;
(3) Busulfex iv 3.2 mg/kgBW/day x 4 days, Cyclophosphamide 60mg/kgBW/day x 2 days
(4) Fludarabine 30 mg/m2/day x 5 days, Busulfex iv 3.2 mg/kgBW/day x 2 days.
